    "title": "Is Home Depot open on Easter?",
    "text": "Weekends are for home projects, and Easter weekend is no different than any other for plenty of Americans. Whether this Sunday includes yard work, closet organizing or other spring cleaning, Home Depot likely has many of the supplies you need to get the jobs done. So you’ll be happy to know that The Home Depot will be open for business on Sunday, April 5. According to the Home Depot website, stores will be open from 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. Home Depot has seen a decline in foot traffic in recent years.Suhail/Getty Images · Suhail&sol;Getty Images Home Depot is one of those stores that rarely closes. In fact, Home Depot only closes two days each year: Thanksgiving Day and Christmas Day. Home Depot, Inc. accounts for 52.4% of the home improvement market ($149.5 billion a year), according to data from IBISWorld. Still, visits to Home Depot have been down, so the company needs to keep its doors open as many days as possible. Home Depot's foot traffic declined about 3.8% year over year in Q1 2026, according to Placer.ai data shared on Yahoo Finance. Home Depot is open on Easter, which is good news if you're planning to tackle home projects. And even though the Home Depot website says stores are open on Easter, use the Home Depot locator to make sure your store is. Plenty of other major retailers are also open. Kroger is open normal hours, but pharmacies are closed. Harris Teeter stores are open normal hours. Meijer stores are open from 6 a.m. to midnight. Stop and Shop locations are open from 7 a.m. to 5 p.m., but pharmacies are closed. Trader Joe’s plans to be open regular business hours. Walmart is open normal hours. Whole Foods locations are open until 6 p.m. Winn-Dixie stores will be open normal business hours. Sources: Store websites Related: Home Depot sees worrisome shift in consumer behavior This story was originally published by TheStreet on Apr 5, 2026, where it first appeared in the Retail section. Add TheStreet as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
